open syncs the parent of a database directory it did not create only when it
created nothing; without it, an entry left unsynced by an open that failed or
was killed stays volatile and a power cut loses the directory and every file
synced in it. Reverts the #740 fix.
Guarded-by: "directory sync: open syncs the entry of a directory that exists"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/db.cpp b/bytecaskdb/db.cpp
index 845f0af..614f96f 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/db.cpp
+++ b/bytecaskdb/db.cpp
@@ -97,10 +97,6 @@ DB::DB(std::filesystem::path dir, Options opts)
   std::filesystem::create_directories(dir_);
   for (const auto &p : created)
     sync_directory(p.parent_path(), "io_dir_sync_create_dir");
-  if (created.empty()) {
-    sync_directory(std::filesystem::absolute(dir_).parent_path(),
-                   "io_dir_sync_create_dir");
-  }
 
   // Acquire exclusive advisory lock on the database directory.
   const auto lock_path = dir_ / ".lock";
